w annually. Stock-based compensation of $49K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 7\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (10/10).","financial_summary":["Navan, Inc. is a mid-cap technology business with a $7.3B market cap on $702M of annual revenue.","Returns on capital run at -33% against a 10% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests. Gross margins of 71% confirm genuine pricing power.","The business throws off $33M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 5 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders.","On the balance sheet, thin -3.8\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and stock-based comp at 26% of revenue is silent dilution an owner has to account for, and insiders hold 20% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 281% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":2.8144279415193427},{"text":"Very elevated short interest (28.0% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting against the business","sev":"red","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Operating margins 35% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $14.6M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Technology sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 9% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Technology ETF trading well below its long-term trend","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Elevated sector volatility (52% annualized) adds uncertainty","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Sector under pressure with a 18.0% decline over the past 6 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Cybersecurity liability and talent cost inflation \u2014 a single breach can erase years of goodwill, and the war for engineering talent compresses margins even at scale.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Valued at a 365% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","Founder-led \u2014 owner alignment that often matters more than any incentive plan"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Navan (NASDAQ:NAVN) Stock Rating Lowered by Wall Street Zen","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/14/navan-nasdaqnavn-stock-rating-lowered-by-wall-street-zen.html","date":"2026-11-14","timestamp":1794648022.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.649,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Oren Zeev Purchases 466 Navan Shares Through RSU at $24.18 Each","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/news/announcements/oren-zeev-purchases-466-navan-shares-through-rsu-at-2418-each","date":"2026-11-25","timestamp":1795569145.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.296,"tier":1,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Navan Director Clara Liang Receives 517 Shares as Board Retainer Compensation","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/news/announcements/navan-director-clara-liang-receives-517-shares-as-board-retainer-compensation","date":"2026-11-24","timestamp":1795560833.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.296,"tier":1,"scope":"company"